# 🎮 Mission Control Complete Feature Architecture & User Guide

Mission Control is an advanced, AI-powered gaming OS environment and co-pilot that unifies modern PC storefronts, standalone emulators, Linux compatibility layers, hardware telemetry, and autonomous system optimizations into a single glassmorphic interface.

---

## 🕹️ 1. Emulation & ROM Library Orchestration Engine

### Cross-Platform Auto-Discovery (17+ Emulators)
Mission Control automatically detects installed standalone emulators and RetroArch libretro cores across standard Windows and Linux installation paths:
- **PlayStation Ecosystem:**
  - **RPCS3 (PS3):** Scans `%LOCALAPPDATA%\RPCS3`, `C:\RPCS3`, `~/.var/app/net.rpcs3.RPCS3`. Supports `.pkg`, `.iso`, and `EBOOT.BIN`.
  - **PCSX2 (PS2):** Scans `%LOCALAPPDATA%\PCSX2`, `C:\PCSX2`, `~/.var/app/net.pcsx2.PCSX2`. Supports `.iso`, `.chd`, `.bin`, `.cue`, `.gz`.
  - **DuckStation (PS1):** Scans `%LOCALAPPDATA%\DuckStation`, `~/.var/app/org.duckstation.DuckStation`. Supports `.chd`, `.cue`, `.iso`, `.pbp`.
  - **Vita3K (PS Vita):** Scans `%APPDATA%\Vita3K`, `C:\Vita3K`. Supports `.vpk`, `.zip`, `.pkg`.
  - **PPSSPP (PSP):** Scans `%PROGRAMFILES%\PPSSPP`, `%APPDATA%\PPSSPP`. Supports `.iso`, `.cso`, `.chd`, `.pbp`.
- **Nintendo Ecosystem:**
  - **Ryujinx (Switch):** Scans `%APPDATA%\Ryujinx`, `~/.config/Ryujinx`. Supports `.nsp`, `.xci`.
  - **Dolphin (GameCube & Wii):** Scans `%APPDATA%\Dolphin Emulator`, `~/.var/app/org.DolphinEmu.dolphin-emu`. Supports `.iso`, `.rvz`, `.wbfs`, `.gcm`.
  - **Cemu (Wii U):** Scans `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Cemu`, `~/.var/app/info.cemu.Cemu`. Supports `.wux`, `.wua`, `.rpx`.
  - **Lime3DS / Citra (3DS):** Scans `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Lime3DS`, `%APPDATA%\Citra`. Supports `.3ds`, `.cia`, `.cxi`.
  - **melonDS (NDS):** Scans `%APPDATA%\melonDS`, `/usr/bin/melonds`. Supports `.nds`, `.bin`.
  - **mGBA (Game Boy Advance):** Scans `%PROGRAMFILES%\mGBA`, `/usr/bin/mgba`. Supports `.gba`, `.zip`.
  - **Snes9x (SNES):** Scans `C:\Snes9x`, `/usr/bin/snes9x-gtk`. Supports `.sfc`, `.smc`, `.zip`.
  - **Mupen64Plus (N64):** Scans `%PROGRAMFILES%\Mupen64Plus`, `/usr/bin/mupen64plus`. Supports `.z64`, `.n64`, `.v64`.
- **Xbox Consoles:**
  - **Xenia & Xenia Canary (Xbox 360):** Scans `C:\Xenia`, `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Xenia`. Supports `.iso`, `.xex`.
  - **Xemu (Original Xbox):** Scans `%APPDATA%\xemu`, `~/.var/app/app.xemu.xemu`. Supports `.iso`, `.xbe`.
- **Sega & Multi-System:**
  - **Flycast (Dreamcast):** Scans `C:\Flycast`, `%APPDATA%\Flycast`. Supports `.cdi`, `.gdi`, `.chd`.
  - **RetroArch:** Scans installed cores in `%APPDATA%\RetroArch\cores` or `~/.config/retroarch/cores`.

### Automated Multi-Disc Merging Engine
Classic multi-disc adventures (e.g. Final Fantasy VII, Metal Gear Solid) conform to pattern heuristics: `(Disc 1)`, `(Disc 2)`, `[CD1]`, `[CD2]`, `_disc1`, `-disc2`.
Mission Control merges these into a single library card with an interactive in-card disc selector dropdown, letting the user choose which disc to boot into the emulator without cluttering the library.

### Custom ROM Folders & Scanning
- Users can add multiple custom ROM directories from different drives (e.g., `D:\Emulation\Roms`, `E:\Backups\PS2`) via the **Emulators & ROMs Hub** -> **ROM Folders** tab.
- Clicking **Scan ROMs Now** initiates recursive directory indexing with real-time progress percentages and toast alerts.

### 1-Click Argument-Aware Execution
Mission Control bypasses launcher UIs by assembling emulator-specific CLI execution arguments:
- RPCS3: Spawns binary with `--no-gui` and direct path to `.pkg` or `EBOOT.BIN`.
- Ryujinx: Launches with `-g <rom_path>` in fullscreen.
- PCSX2: Passes `-batch -fullscreen <rom_path>`.
- Dolphin: Passes `-b -e <rom_path>`.
- RetroArch: Dynamically resolves matching libretro `.dll`/`.so` core and passes `-L <core_path> <rom_path>`.

### Adjacent Cover Art Resolution
Scans adjacent directory structures for boxart: `<rom_stem>.png`, `<base_title>.png`, `media/boxart/`, `covers/` before falling back to cloud art or SVG placeholders.

