## 🍷 2. Linux Wine & Proton Compatibility Engine

### Architecture & Runner Management
Mission Control provides first-class compatibility orchestration for running Windows games on Linux distributions (Steam Deck, Bazzite, Ubuntu, Fedora, Arch):
- **Runner Selection:** Users can choose between **GE-Proton**, **Proton Experimental**, **Wine-GE**, and system **Wine** on a per-game basis in the Game Details *Compatibility* drawer.
- **Isolated Sandboxed Prefixes:** Every Windows title receives an isolated `WINEPREFIX` directory (`~/.local/share/mission-control/prefixes/<game-slug>`), preventing registry pollution and cross-game DLL conflicts.
- **DirectX-to-Vulkan Translation:** Employs **DXVK 2.4+** (Direct3D 9/10/11) and **VKD3D-Proton** (DirectX 12) with asynchronous shader pipelines for stutter-free performance.
- **Per-Game Overrides:** Configurable DLL overrides (`d3d11`, `dxgi`, `dsound`), launch command parameters (`gamemoderun %command%`), GameScope scaling, MangoHud overlays, and FSR upscaling.
- **Launch Error Diagnostics:** A background stdout/stderr log scanner analyzes startup crashes, detects missing runtime dependencies (.NET Framework, Visual C++ Redistributables, DirectX), and offers 1-click remediation hints.

---

## 🖥️ 3. Hardware Telemetry & GPU MUX Switch

### GPU MUX Switch Status
Mission Control detects and reports display routing telemetry:
- **Discrete GPU Mode (dGPU):** Display panel is directly connected to the dedicated NVIDIA/AMD GPU, bypassing the integrated GPU. This delivers maximum framerates, lowest latency, and G-Sync/FreeSync support.
- **Hybrid / Optimus Mode:** Frames rendered by the discrete GPU are routed through the integrated CPU graphics (iGPU) to the internal display, which introduces slight latency and framerate overhead but conserves battery.
- The user can check MUX switch status in the **Hardware Optimization** / **System** panel.

### Live Metrics & Thermal Advisor
- Tracks real-time FPS, Frametime sparkline graphs, 1% low and 0.1% low framerate pacing.
- Monitors VRAM allocation, CPU/GPU utilization, and temperatures.
- Proactively surfaces thermal advisor warnings when GPU exceeds 85°C, and critical alerts at 90°C+ to recommend fan curves or undervolting.

---

## ⚡ 4. Agentic Mode & System Actions

### Autonomous vs Observing Interlocks
The **Agentic Mode** toggle in the sidebar navigation controls the AI co-pilot's authorization level:
- **When Agentic Mode is ON (Autonomous):** Aero can directly modify system settings and launch games using structured command tags:
  - `[SYSTEM_COMMAND:optimize_game_mode]` — Sets high process priority, clears standby memory, and enables high-performance power plan.
  - `[SYSTEM_COMMAND:set_fan_profile:performance]` — Adjusts thermal fan curve profile.
  - `[SYSTEM_COMMAND:clear_standby_list]` — Flushes Windows standby memory to free up RAM.
  - `[LAUNCH_COMMAND:<game_name>]` — Directly executes PC games, storefront launchers, or emulated ROMs.
- **When Agentic Mode is OFF (Observing):** Aero runs in safe advisory mode. Direct system commands are blocked or present an interactive confirmation interlock toast to the user before executing.

---

## 📚 5. Unified Game Intelligence Library & Storefronts
- Merges PC games from Steam, Epic Games, GOG Galaxy, Xbox Game Pass, EA Desktop, Ubisoft Connect, and standalone setups with console emulated games into one responsive glassmorphic library.
- Offers instant smart filters: All, PC, Emulation, VR, Installed, and Genre.
- Synchronizes game taxonomy, play sessions, and keybindings with local SQLite cache.

---

## 🧪 6. Stability Lab & Benchmarks
- Automated stress tests and crash diagnostics.
- Post-session performance summaries: average FPS, 1% lows, GPU utilization peaks, and thermal curves after closing a game.
